@startuml m1-incident-lifecycle
title Incident lifecycle (Member 1): IncidentStatus transitions
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam state {
  BackgroundColor #EFF6FF
  BorderColor #2563EB
}

[*] --> NEW : IncidentFactory.create()\n[IncidentReported]

NEW --> CLASSIFIED : classify()\n[system, or any non-employee]
NEW --> MERGED : mergeInto(parent)

CLASSIFIED --> ASSIGNED : assignTo()\n[system, team lead, admin, IT manager]\n[IncidentAssigned]
CLASSIFIED --> MERGED : mergeInto(parent)
CLASSIFIED : applyPriority(), startSla()
CLASSIFIED : flagAwaitingAssignment() when nobody is free

ASSIGNED --> ACKNOWLEDGED : acknowledge()\n[assignee]\n/ sla.markResponded()
ASSIGNED --> ASSIGNED : assignTo() (reassign)

ACKNOWLEDGED --> IN_PROGRESS : startWork()\n[assignee]
ACKNOWLEDGED --> ASSIGNED : assignTo() (reassign)

IN_PROGRESS --> PENDING_INFO : requestInfo(question)\n[assignee]\n/ sla.pause()
IN_PROGRESS --> RESOLVED : resolve(summary, rootCause)\n[assignee]\n/ sla.pause()

PENDING_INFO --> IN_PROGRESS : provideInfo(answer)\n[reporter]\n/ sla.resume()
PENDING_INFO : SLA clock paused

RESOLVED --> VERIFIED : verify()\n[reporter or system]
RESOLVED --> IN_PROGRESS : reopen(reason)\n[reporter]\n/ discardResolution(), sla.resume()
RESOLVED : SLA clock paused

VERIFIED --> CLOSED : close()\n[assignee, team lead, admin,\nIT manager or system]

CLOSED : terminal; submitFeedback() once [reporter]
MERGED : terminal; duplicateOfId = parent

CLOSED --> [*]
MERGED --> [*]

note "Any action not on an arrow → 409 InvalidStateTransitionException; state unchanged.\nWhile open: addNote(), joinAsAffected(), markSlaWarning(), markSlaBreached(), escalate()\nchange no status. On CLOSED or MERGED they are rejected (409); submitFeedback() is the\nonly action allowed on CLOSED." as N1
@enduml
